  "content": "Given a rectangle with perimeter $P = 30$ and length $L = 9$, the width $W$ is calculated as:\n\n$$W = \\frac{P}{2} - L = \\frac{30}{2} - 9 = 15 - 9 = 6$$\n\nThe area $A$ is:\n\n$$A = L \\times W = 9 \\times 6 = 54$$\n\nThus, the width is 6 and the area is 54.",
